From: alvesmaicon <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: sun6i-prcm: give the A23 codec its headset detection registers

The A23/A33 analog codec has a headset detection block right after its
PR register: an enable at 0x1c4, a control register at 0x1c8 and a data
register at 0x1cc, with the headset mic ADC and the jack interrupt
flags. The vendor kernel's switch driver uses it. Extend the codec's
resource from 4 to 16 bytes so its driver can reach them.

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/sun6i-prcm.c b/drivers/mfd/sun6i-prcm.c
--- a/drivers/mfd/sun6i-prcm.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/sun6i-prcm.c
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
 #include <linux/of.h>
 
 #define SUN8I_CODEC_ANALOG_BASE	0x1c0
-#define SUN8I_CODEC_ANALOG_SIZE	0x4
+#define SUN8I_CODEC_ANALOG_SIZE	0x10
 
 struct prcm_data {
 	int nsubdevs;
